ion":1,"item":{"@id":"https://www.airroi.com/","name":"Home"}},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"item":{"@id":"https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data","name":"Airbnb Data"}},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"item":{"@id":"https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/world","name":"World"}},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"item":{"@id":"https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states","name":"United States"}},{"@type":"ListItem","position":5,"item":{"@id":"https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina","name":"South Carolina"}},{"@type":"ListItem","position":6,"item":{"@id":"https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/myrtle-beach","name":"Myrtle Beach"}}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/myrtle-beach#faq","url":"https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/myrtle-beach","mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/myrtle-beach"},"isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/myrtle-beach"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much do Airbnb hosts make in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An active Myrtle Beach Airbnb grossed $25,807 on average in the 12 months to September 2026, according to AirROI's tracking of 8,698 active listings. That is before cleaning, management, taxes and financing. Busier, better-run listings do far better: the top quarter took in $4,330 or more in a typical month."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much can I make on Airbnb in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends most on the home's size, location and how it's run. The middle half of Myrtle Beach listings earn between $1,270 and $4,330 in a typical month, and the top tenth $6,770 or more. For one home, enter its address and bedroom count in the Airbnb income calculator: it compares the home with similar listings nearby."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the average Airbnb occupancy rate in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Listings in Myrtle Beach were booked on 36% of available nights over the past year. That compares with 39% for the South Carolina average. July is usually the busiest month."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does an Airbnb cost per night in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The average booked night in Myrtle Beach cost $257 before fees. Half of listings charge between $160 and $285, so bedroom count and location move the price more than the average suggests."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you need a permit for an Airbnb in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, in the zones that allow stays under 90 days, with a City of Myrtle Beach business license; most residential neighborhoods are closed to short-term rentals. The Myrtle Beach Airbnb regulations set out the permit, its cost, the taxes on a stay and the operating limits, each linked to its official source."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Airbnb profitable in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, when it's run well. The average Myrtle Beach Airbnb grossed $25,807 in the 12 months to September 2026, 31% below the South Carolina average of $37,525. Run by its owner, with the cleaning fee covering the cleaner and everyday costs for Airbnb's fee, utilities, supplies, upkeep and insurance, $15,977 a year (about $1,330 a month) is left before the mortgage or rent. A home that costs less than that to own or rent makes a profit, and a listing at the top-quarter mark leaves about $2,310 a month. Check a specific home in the Airbnb estimator."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When is Airbnb peak season in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"July usually pays best, averaging $6,800 per active listing over the past two years, and January usually pays least. The month-by-month table above shows how the latest 12 months played out."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Airbnb RevPAR in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Each night a Myrtle Beach listing was open to book earned $106 on average over the past year, booked or not. That figure, revenue per available night (RevPAR), folds price and occupancy into one number; the top 10% of listings made $204 or more."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How far in advance do guests book Airbnbs in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Myrtle Beach stays were booked 52 days (about seven weeks) before arrival on average over the past year, so most of a month is booked well before it starts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long do guests stay at Airbnbs in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The average Myrtle Beach Airbnb stay lasted 4.7 nights over the past year. A listing took 19 reservations over the year on average."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How are Airbnbs in Myrtle Beach rated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Guests rate Myrtle Beach Airbnbs 4.66 out of 5 on average. Guests score location highest and cleanliness lowest."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the best neighborhoods for Airbnb in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Broadway at the Beach, Myrtle Beach Boardwalk and Promenade and West Myrtle Beach draw the most short-term rental interest in Myrtle Beach. The neighborhood guide explains what brings guests to each."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many Airbnbs are there in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"AirROI counted 8,698 active Airbnb listings in Myrtle Beach as of September 2026. The closest tracked market is Fantasy Harbour, 5 km away."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much are Airbnb cleaning fees in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In Myrtle Beach, about nine in ten listings add a cleaning fee, and the typical fee is about $151."}}]},{"@type":"Place","@id